@@ -15,3 +15,18 @@ resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
 `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the value a pointer refers to. It throws if the pointer is not
 a valid RFC 6901 pointer, or does not resolve to a value (missing member, out-of-range or non-canonical
 array index, `-`, or descending into a primitive). Only own members are resolved; the document is not mutated.
+
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "./src/index.js";
+
+applyPatch({ foo: "bar" }, [{ op: "add", path: "/baz", value: "qux" }]); // { foo: "bar", baz: "qux" }
+```
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies an array of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`
+operations and returns the result as a new value; neither the document nor the patch is mutated, and the
+result shares no structure with them. It throws if the patch is invalid (not an array, unknown `op`,
+missing or invalid `path`, `from` or `value`) or an operation fails (unresolvable path, failed `test`,
+`move` into its own child, removing the root). The patch is atomic: on error nothing is returned.
+Notes: `-` and `0..length` indexes work for `add`; `"__proto__"` and similar are ordinary keys.
