+---
+id: task-002-json-patch-applypatch-rfc-6902
+type: task
+title: "JSON Patch applyPatch RFC 6902"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Task: JSON Patch, RFC 6902
+
+Export `applyPatch(document, patch)` from `src/index.ts`. It applies a JSON Patch (an array of
+operations) and returns the result as a new value; the input document and the patch are never mutated
+and the result shares no structure with them. It throws if the patch is invalid or an operation fails;
+the patch is atomic (no partial result is returned).
+
+Governing standard: RFC 6902 (sections 3 format, 4 operations, 5 error handling), paths per RFC 6901.
+
+- Patch must be an array of objects with a string `op` among add, remove, replace, move, copy, test and
+  a string `path`; `value` required (own, not undefined) for add/replace/test; `from` string for move/copy.
+- add: parent must exist; array index `0..length` or `-` inserts (shifting), object member is set or
+  replaced; `""` replaces the whole document (4.1).
+- remove: target must exist; arrays shift; removing the root throws (4.2).
+- replace: target must exist (4.3). move: `from` must exist and must not be a proper prefix of `path`
+  (4.4). copy: deep copy of the `from` value (4.5).
+- test: deep equality (objects unordered, arrays ordered, numbers by value, types must match) (4.6).
+- Prototype pollution: `__proto__`, `constructor`, `prototype` are plain keys, only own members are read.
+- Tests in `test/` cover the RFC's appendix A examples and error cases.
